    {
      "id": "C-REVOKE-1",
      "text": "Sessions issued inside the propagation window (the assumed 30 s before the cutoff) are covered by the deny."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-REVOKE-2",
      "text": "Sessions issued after the cutoff are not covered; a role that can still be assumed yields new sessions."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-REVOKE-3",
      "text": "The deny applies to every user of the role, including legitimate sessions issued before the cutoff."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-REVOKE-4",
      "text": "Service-linked roles cannot be revoked this way."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-REVOKE-5",
      "text": "Derived credentials (chained role sessions, access keys created by the session, secrets already read) are not affected by the deny; role chaining is not modelled, so they are listed as residual_unknown."
